{"text": "fourteen", "etymologies": [{"etymologyHTML": "<p>From Middle English <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"enm\">fourtene</i>, from Old English <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"ang\">f\u0113owert\u012bene</i>, from Proto-Germanic <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"gem-pro\">*fedurtehun</i>. Cognate with West Frisian <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"fy\">fjirtjin</i>, Dutch <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"nl\">veertien</i>, German <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"de\">vierzehn</i>, Danish <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"da\">fjorten</i>. Equivalent to <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\">four</i> +\u200e <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\">-teen</i>.\n</p>", "pos": []}], "pronunciation": [["UK", "/\u02ccf\u0254\u02d0\u02c8ti\u02d0n/"], ["UK", "/\u02c8f\u0254\u02d0.ti\u02d0n/"]]}